# data-models-relationships

## Core Data Models

The system revolves around the following key entities and their relationships:

1. Defendants
- Connected to bond compliance records
- Associated with jurisdiction/county data
- Linked to GPS check-in history and photo verifications

2. Compliance Records
- Tracks bond verification status
- Stores GPS coordinates and accuracy data
- Contains photo verification timestamps
- Links to SMS notification history

3. Agent Records
- Maps to jurisdiction assignments
- Contains warm transfer capabilities
- Stores case context for whisper functionality

4. Location Data
- Geolocation verification points
- Accuracy radius calculations 
- VPN/proxy detection flags
- Multi-provider verification status

5. Communication Records
- Multi-provider message delivery status
- Jurisdiction-specific routing data
- One-time token associations
- SMS template mappings

## Key Relationships

1. Defendant -> Compliance
- One-to-many relationship tracking verification events
- Links GPS data to photo submissions
- Maps notification attempts and responses

2. Agent -> Jurisdiction
- Many-to-many mapping for coverage
- Links to warm transfer capabilities
- Associates case context data

3. Location -> Compliance
- One-to-one mapping per verification event
- Ties accuracy data to compliance checks
- Links proxy detection results

4. Communication -> Defendant
- One-to-many tracking of notifications
- Maps provider delivery status
- Links verification tokens

